# README and GitHub Release writing

Canon (accepted style): root `README.md` and
[v2.0.0](https://github.com/lqdflying/chathub/releases/tag/v2.0.0).
If unsure, skim a current **Immich** major (Highlights one-liners first) and
[Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) — do not invent an essay.

## Surfaces

| Surface | Job |
| --- | --- |
| Root `README.md` | Product landing: what this GA *is*, not a wiki index |
| GitHub Release | Scannable announcement for **one** tag |
| Wiki Home | Short story + small table, then **procedure index** |
| Wiki feature pages | How to configure / operate |
| OpenWiki | Maintainer internals — not a marketing landing |

Do not copy one surface onto another.

## Never

- Concatenate prior GitHub Release bodies or list GAs one by one
- Dump `git log` / PR titles as the notes
- Huge paragraphs or thematic essays
- A 16-row comparison table or a bullet for every feature
- Sell v1.0.0 table-stakes (credentials login, Tools Hub, MCP OAuth, gear) as if they were new

Cover the **substance** of the range (`vPREV...vNEW`). Understand, then summarize.

## README (major)

1. Two–four sentence opener: this GA vs last first-GA, upgrade path
2. **Five or fewer** highlights: `**Claim.**` + one short paragraph + wiki link
3. Comparison table: **≤5 rows**, only deltas vs upstream / previous contract
4. Operator Quick Start (Compose / auth / env) stays here
5. Catalog and procedures stay on the wiki

Patch README edits: one short paragraph or a few bullets — do not rewrite the landing.

## GitHub Release

```markdown
<2–3 sentence opener: what this tag is, upgrade in one line, versioning gotchas>

## Highlights
- one line per item (scan this first)

## Upgrade
- image tag, migrations, sidecar/env gotchas
- wiki link

## Added / Changed / Removed   (or ## Fixed on a patch)
- one-line bullets, grouped by area (Chat, Knowledge, Tools, …)

## Docs
- wiki links, not explanations

Full diff: https://github.com/lqdflying/chathub/compare/vPREV...vNEW
```

- **Major:** Highlights = product contract change. Keep a Changelog sections for the rest.
- **Patch:** Highlights + Fixed. Skip a 2.0-style landing.
- One `> [!NOTE]` or `> [!WARNING]` max unless upgrade truly needs two.
- `gh release edit` to fix notes; do not retag.

Style: [git-and-release.mdc](git-and-release.mdc) (when to create the release).
GFM: GitHub Markdown skill (alerts, tables, no wiki footnotes).
